{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/instruction.md /workspace/task.toml /workspace/environment/public_eval/grader.py /workspace/environment/public_eval/worker.py'","aggregated_output":"# Exact Multihead Retrieval Kernel\n\n## Goal\nImplement a CPU tensor algorithm that computes the operator below and minimizes inference latency. Inputs are float32 features, three per-head linear maps and two scalar controls. A valid submission is a pure `attention` function in `/workspace/solution/method.py` that satisfies the numerical contract for unseen inputs.\n\n## Task Setting\nThe environment contains Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.5.1 and NumPy 2.2.6. No training, downloaded weights or external data are required. A direct correct Starter is available read-only at `/workspace/environment/starter/method.py`; the writable initial solution copies this Starter. Public generated inputs and the public scoring program are available under `/workspace/environment/`. Final verification uses separately generated private inputs in an independent environment after the final solution is transferred.\n\n## Objective and Metrics\nLet `x` have shape `(B,L,C)` and each map `wq,wk,wv` have shape `(H,D,C)`. For each head define `q=x wq^T`, `k=x wk^T`, `A=q k^T / sqrt(D)`, `P0=softmax(A)` and `P1=softmax(((1+alpha)/2) A + ((1-alpha)/2) A^T)` along the last axis. Define `u0=P0 x`, `u1=P1 x`, `m=u0+beta*(u1-u0)` and `r=clamp(max(||u1||_2,1e-6)/max(||m||_2,1e-6),0.25,4.0)` per head and token. Return the concatenated head outputs `(r*m) wv^T` in shape `(B,L,H*D)`. There are no linear biases or final output map in this operator.\n\nEvery output must be finite float32 CPU with the specified shape and satisfy elementwise `abs(actual-expected) <= 3e-5 + 3e-4*abs(expected)`. Inputs must not be modified. Tensor computation is permitted; changing the operator is prohibited. PyTorch runs with one intra-op and inter-op thread. For each case, the candidate and the protected healthy Starter control are independently measured using process CPU execution time in milliseconds (`time.process_time_ns`): median of 11 measured calls after 3 warmups per case, arithmetic mean across cases, then arithmetic mean across seeds `[17,29,43,71,101]`. The raw metric is the arithmetic mean of per-case candidate/control CPU-time ratios, then the arithmetic mean across seeds. The control is freshly measured in the same evaluation with identical inputs and budgets, so each result compares methods under the same hardware conditions, rather than using a millisecond anchor measured on another machine. Lower is better. Timing is stochastic; a claimed improvement must exceed three times the Baseline sample standard deviation across the five complete paired seed runs. Case generation is deterministic per seed. Wall-clock latency is reported separately as a diagnostic; scheduling and CPU quota delays are excluded from the primary CPU time metric.\n\nThe continuous score is `(B_latency - measured_latency)/(B_latency - U_latency)`, without clipping. `U_latency=0` is the mathematical ratio floor, not a Reference result. The calibrated split-specific Baseline anchor is stored in the protected protocol. The calibrated ratio anchor comes from all five complete formal Baseline runs. The public five-seed Baseline ratio anchor is 1.06765098401. Private evaluation uses its own protected split-specific Baseline ratio anchor. Numerical errors and constraint violations produce invalid score `-1`; malformed submissions, timeouts, resource failures and infrastructure failures are separate diagnostic states and do not masquerade as zero performance.\n\n## Allowed Scope\nOnly `/workspace/solution/method.py` may be modified. Implement `attention(x,wq,wk,wv,alpha,beta)` returning a tensor. Helpers and arbitrary algebraic rearrangements using CPU PyTorch and math are allowed. Decorators are limited to PyTorch no_grad/inference_mode contexts; custom persistent-state decorators and mutable defaults are forbidden. Read the Starter, public protocol and public evaluator. Run `/workspace/solution/solve.sh` for Dev evaluation and read `/workspace/public-results/result.json`. Final verification recomputes outputs and timings; candidate-reported scores are not accepted.\n\n## Hard Boundaries\nThe method file must be a regular file of at most 256 KiB. Imports are limited to `torch` and `math`. Filesystem access, process creation, introspection, dynamic execution, runtime/thread reconfiguration, mutable module/function state, persistent result caching, external communication and input mutation are forbidden. The source guard and protected worker implement the restrictions; Docker limits each environment to one CPU and 2 GiB memory. Networking is disabled during verification; the Coding Agent phase permits only the two configured model inference hosts for its CLI. Research web search and network tools are prohibited; local shell tools may inspect public files and invoke Dev evaluation only. Each benchmark case has a 120-second timeout and the complete evaluation has a 1800-second limit. Protected programs and data cannot be modified. Never access final private evaluation assets or another model's results.\n\n## Submission Instructions\nKeep `/workspace/solution/method.py` and the frozen `/workspace/solution/solve.sh`. The function takes six positional arguments; scalar controls are Python floats. There is no submission JSON or model checkpoint. Harbor transfers `/workspace/solution` to its original path in the independent Verifier, which validates source and directly executes the candidate. Additional files and self-reported scores are ignored.\n\n## Workflow & Iteration\nThis is an anytime task. Implement a method, run the protected public evaluator, inspect correctness and measured latency, and retain or revert using those results. Whenever a better valid method is found, replace `method.py` with that current best; the most recent valid submission is scored. Typical Dev evaluation is intended to finish in minutes and must stay within the complete evaluation budget. Preserve the current best before experimenting, then restore it before completion.\n\n## Completion Criteria\nThe final method respects the fixed operator, passes the source guard and all numerical gates, produces a finite measured score with the calibrated protocol, and reruns from a clean snapshot. Protected files remain unchanged and final private inputs have not been accessed during optimization.\nschema_version = \"1.4\"\nartifacts = [\"/workspace/solution\"]\n\n[task]\nname = \"autoresearch/exact-retrieval-kernel\"\nversion = \"0.2.3\"\ndescription = \"Optimize a norm-preserving multihead retrieval operator under fixed numerical semantics.\"\nauthors = [{name = \"AutoResearch Expert\"}]\n\n[metadata]\ncategory = \"numerical-algorithms\"\npath_contract = \"harbor-environment-v1\"\ndifficulty_explanation = \"Algorithm implementation is open; latency is scored only after numerical correctness. Baseline calibrated from all five formal seed runs.\"\n\n[agent]\nuser = \"agent\"\ntimeout_sec = 50400\nnetwork_mode = \"allowlist\"\nallowed_hosts = [\"modcon.top\", \"ark.cn-beijing.volces.com\"]\n\n[environment]\ncpus = 1\nmemory_mb = 2048\nstorage_mb = 4096\nnetwork_mode = \"no-network\"\nworkdir = \"/workspace\"\nbuild_timeout_sec = 1800\n\n[verifier]\nenvironment_mode = \"separate\"\nuser = \"root\"\ntimeout_sec = 1800\n\n[verifier.environment]\ncpus = 1\nmemory_mb = 2048\nstorage_mb = 4096\nnetwork_mode = \"no-network\"\nworkdir = \"/tests\"\n\"\"\"Trusted public benchmark; Hidden uses an independent copy and private protocol.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport ast\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport resource\nimport shutil\nimport statistics\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n\n\nclass Invalid(Exception):\n    def __init__(self, kind, message):\n        self.kind, self.message = kind, message\n\n\ndef check_source(path):\n    if path.is_symlink() or not path.is_file():\n        raise Invalid(\"format_error\", \"Submit a regular method.py file.\")\n    if path.stat().st_size > 262144:\n        raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"method.py exceeds 256 KiB.\")\n    try:\n        tree = ast.parse(path.read_text())\n    except (SyntaxError, UnicodeError) as e:\n        raise Invalid(\"format_error\", str(e))\n    banned = {\"open\", \"eval\", \"exec\", \"compile\", \"__import__\", \"getattr\", \"setattr\", \"delattr\",\n              \"globals\", \"locals\", \"vars\", \"dir\", \"input\", \"breakpoint\", \"memoryview\"}\n    torch_names = {\"torch\"}\n    safe_context_names = set()\n    for node in tree.body:\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Import):\n            torch_names.update(a.asname or a.name for a in node.names if a.name == \"torch\")\n        elif isinstance(node, ast.ImportFrom) and node.module == \"torch\":\n            safe_context_names.update(a.asname or a.name for a in node.names if a.name in {\"no_grad\", \"inference_mode\"})\n    bad_attrs = {\"load\", \"save\", \"from_file\", \"frombuffer\", \"set_num_threads\", \"set_num_interop_threads\",\n                 \"set_default_device\", \"set_default_dtype\", \"set_grad_enabled\", \"set_flush_denormal\",\n                 \"set_num_interop_threads\", \"set_rng_state\", \"manual_seed\", \"seed\", \"initial_seed\",\n                 \"ops\", \"classes\", \"distributed\", \"multiprocessing\", \"hub\", \"utils\", \"jit\", \"compile\",\n                 \"serialization\", \"cuda\", \"mps\", \"xpu\", \"profiler\", \"benchmark\", \"random\", \"backends\",\n                 \"as_strided\", \"storage\", \"untyped_storage\", \"data_ptr\"}\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(node, (ast.Global, ast.Nonlocal, ast.ClassDef)):\n            raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Persistent state and class-based caches are forbidden.\")\n        if isinstance(node, (ast.Assign, ast.AnnAssign, ast.AugAssign)):\n            targets = node.targets if isinstance(node, ast.Assign) else [node.target]\n            if any(isinstance(t, ast.Attribute) for t in targets):\n                raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Modifying module or function attributes is forbidden.\")\n        if isinstance(node, (ast.Import, ast.ImportFrom)):\n            modules = ([a.name.split(\".\")[0] for a in node.names] if isinstance(node, ast.Import)\n                       else [(node.module or \"\").split(\".\")[0]])\n            if any(m not in {\"torch\", \"math\"} for m in modules) or getattr(node, \"level\", 0):\n                raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Imports are limited to torch and math.\")\n            imported = [(node.module or \"\")] if isinstance(node, ast.ImportFrom) else [a.name for a in node.names]\n            if any(part in bad_attrs for name in imported for part in name.split(\".\")):\n                raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"This PyTorch subsystem is outside the allowed computation surface.\")\n            if isinstance(node, ast.ImportFrom) and any(a.name in bad_attrs or a.name == \"*\" or a.name.startswith(\"_\") for a in node.names):\n                raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"This imported function is forbidden.\")\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Name) and (node.id in banned or node.id.startswith(\"__\")):\n            raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Filesystem, reflection and dynamic execution are forbidden.\")\n        if isinstance(node, ast.Attribute) and (node.attr in bad_attrs or node.attr.startswith(\"_\")):\n            raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Candidate must use ordinary CPU tensor computation only.\")\n    if not any(isinstance(n, (ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)) and n.name == \"attention\" for n in tree.body):\n        raise Invalid(\"format_error\", \"Define attention(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta).\")\n    for node in tree.body:\n        if not isinstance(node, (ast.Import, ast.ImportFrom, ast.FunctionDef, ast.Assign, ast.AnnAssign)):\n            if not (isinstance(node, ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.value, ast.Constant)):\n                raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Module scope may contain only imports, functions and literal constants.\")\n        if isinstance(node, (ast.Assign, ast.AnnAssign)) and not isinstance(node.value, ast.Constant):\n            raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Module-level mutable state is forbidden.\")\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef):\n            defaults = node.args.defaults + [v for v in node.args.kw_defaults if v is not None]\n            if any(not isinstance(v, ast.Constant) for v in defaults):\n                raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Mutable function-default state is forbidden.\")\n            for decorator in node.decorator_list:\n                func = decorator.func if isinstance(decorator, ast.Call) else decorator\n                safe = ((isinstance(func, ast.Attribute) and isinstance(func.value, ast.Name)\n                         and func.value.id in torch_names and func.attr in {\"no_grad\", \"inference_mode\"})\n                        or (isinstance(func, ast.Name) and func.id in safe_context_names))\n                if not safe:\n                    raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Custom stateful decorators are forbidden; use ordinary pure helpers.\")\n\n\ndef generate(case, seed):\n    g = torch.Generator().manual_seed(seed)\n    b, l, c, h, d = (case[k] for k in (\"batch\", \"length\", \"channels\", \"heads\", \"dim\"))\n    x = torch.randn(b, l, c, generator=g) * case.get(\"input_scale\", 1.)\n    if case.get(\"degenerate\") == \"zero\":\n        x.zero_()\n    weights = [torch.randn(h, d, c, generator=g) / math.sqrt(c) for _ in range(3)]\n    return x, *weights, case[\"alpha\"], case[\"beta\"]\n\n\ndef oracle(values):\n    x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta = values\n    q = torch.einsum(\"blc,hdc->bhld\", x, wq)\n    k = torch.einsum(\"blc,hdc->bhld\", x, wk)\n    logits = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2) / math.sqrt(wq.shape[1])\n    p0 = logits.softmax(-1)\n    p1 = (.5 * (1 + alpha) * logits + .5 * (1 - alpha) * logits.transpose(-1, -2)).softmax(-1)\n    base, modified = p0 @ x.unsqueeze(1), p1 @ x.unsqueeze(1)\n    mix = base + beta * (modified - base)\n    ratio = (modified.norm(dim=-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-6)\n             / mix.norm(dim=-1, keepdim=True).clamp_min(1e-6)).clamp(.25, 4.)\n    return torch.einsum(\"bhlc,hdc->bhld\", mix * ratio, wv).transpose(1, 2).flatten(2).contiguous()\n\n\ndef worker_limits():\n    os.setsid()\n    resource.setrlimit(resource.RLIMIT_CPU, (110, 110))\n    resource.setrlimit(resource.RLIMIT_FSIZE, (256 * 1024 * 1024, 256 * 1024 * 1024))\n    resource.setrlimit(resource.RLIMIT_NOFILE, (128, 128))\n    if os.getuid() == 0:\n        os.setgroups([])\n        os.setgid(1002)\n        os.setuid(1002)\n\n\ndef run_case(source, values, protocol, scratch):\n    input_path = scratch / \"input.npz\"\n    output_path = scratch / \"output.npz\"\n    # The prior input is read-only. Replace it instead of attempting to reopen it\n    # for writing when public grading runs as the unprivileged Agent user.\n    input_path.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n    arrays = {name: t.numpy() for name, t in zip((\"x\", \"wq\", \"wk\", \"wv\"), values[:4])}\n    np.savez(input_path, **arrays, alpha=values[4], beta=values[5],\n             warmup=protocol[\"warmup\"], repeats=protocol[\"timed_repeats\"])\n    input_path.chmod(0o444)\n    output_path.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n    try:\n        p = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-I\", str(ROOT / \"worker.py\"), str(source),\n                            str(input_path), str(output_path)], cwd=scratch,\n                           env={\"PATH\": os.environ.get(\"PATH\", \"/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin\"),\n                                \"HOME\": str(scratch), \"OMP_NUM_THREADS\": \"1\", \"OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS\": \"1\",\n                                \"MKL_NUM_THREADS\": \"1\", \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE\": \"1\"},\n                           preexec_fn=worker_limits, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n        raise Invalid(\"timeout\", \"One case exceeded 120 seconds.\")\n    if p.returncode != 0:\n        for line in p.stdout.splitlines():\n            try:\n                report = json.loads(line)\n            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                continue\n            if report.get(\"worker_failure\") in {\"hard_gate\", \"format_error\"}:\n                raise Invalid(report[\"worker_failure\"], report[\"message\"])\n        kind = \"resource_error\" if p.returncode < 0 else \"candidate_error\"\n        raise Invalid(kind, p.stderr[-2000:])\n    if not output_path.is_file() or output_path.is_symlink() or output_path.stat().st_size > 256 * 1024 * 1024:\n        raise Invalid(\"format_error\", \"Worker did not produce a valid output array.\")\n    data = np.load(output_path, allow_pickle=False)\n    if not bool(data[\"input_unchanged\"]):\n        raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Candidate modified input tensors.\")\n    actual = torch.from_numpy(data[\"output\"].copy())\n    expected = oracle(values)\n    if actual.shape != expected.shape or actual.dtype != expected.dtype or not torch.isfinite(actual).all():\n        raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Output shape, dtype or finiteness failed.\")\n    if not torch.allclose(actual, expected, **protocol[\"quality\"]):\n        raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", f\"Numerical correctness failed; max abs error={float((actual-expected).abs().max()):.8g}.\")\n    samples = data[\"samples\"].tolist()\n    if len(samples) != protocol[\"timed_repeats\"] or not all(math.isfinite(t) and t > 0 for t in samples):\n        raise Invalid(\"format_error\", \"Invalid timing samples.\")\n    return {\"latency_ms\": statistics.median(samples), \"samples_ms\": samples,\n            \"wall_latency_ms\": statistics.median(data[\"wall_samples\"].tolist()),\n            \"wall_samples_ms\": data[\"wall_samples\"].tolist(),\n            \"max_abs_error\": float((actual - expected).abs().max())}\n\n\ndef atomic_json(path, data):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    tmp = path.with_suffix(path.suffix + \".tmp\")\n    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2, allow_nan=False))\n    tmp.replace(path)\n\n\ndef main():\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    p.add_argument(\"--method\", type=Path, default=Path(\"/workspace/solution/method.py\"))\n    p.add_argument(\"--protocol\", type=Path, default=Path(\"/workspace/environment/public_assets/dev/protocol.json\"))\n    p.add_argument(\"--output\", type=Path, default=Path(\"/workspace/public-results/result.json\"))\n    p.add_argument(\"--seeds\", type=int, nargs=\"+\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--raw-only\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Expert calibration only; no normalized score.\")\n    args = p.parse_args()\n    args.output.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n    started = time.time()\n    try:\n        if args.method == Path(\"/workspace/solution/method.py\"):\n            frozen = ROOT / \"solve.sh\"\n            submitted = args.method.parent / \"solve.sh\"\n            if submitted.is_symlink() or not submitted.is_file() or submitted.read_bytes() != frozen.read_bytes():\n                raise Invalid(\"hard_gate\", \"Restore the frozen solve.sh before submitting.\")\n        check_source(args.method)\n        protocol = json.loads(args.protocol.read_text())\n        torch.set_num_threads(protocol[\"torch_threads\"])\n        torch.set_num_interop_threads(1)\n        records = []\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"attention-worker-\") as temp:\n            scratch = Path(temp)\n            scratch.chmod(0o755)\n            source = scratch / \"method.py\"\n            shutil.copyfile(args.method, source)\n            source.chmod(0o444)\n            outdir = scratch / \"out\"\n            outdir.mkdir()\n            if os.getuid() == 0:\n                os.chown(outdir, 1002, 1002)\n            with torch.inference_mode():\n                for seed in args.seeds or protocol[\"formal_seeds\"]:\n                    per_case = []\n                    for i, case in enumerate(protocol[\"cases\"]):\n                        values = generate(case, seed * 1009 + i)\n                        # Both measurements run the same protected launcher and budgets.\n                        # A fresh healthy control removes CPU architecture and speed as a score advantage.\n                        control = ROOT / \"baseline_method.py\"\n                        if seed % 2:\n                            baseline_record = run_case(control, values, protocol, outdir)\n                            record = run_case(source, values, protocol, outdir)\n                        else:\n                            record = run_case(source, values, protocol, outdir)\n                            baseline_record = run_case(control, values, protocol, outdir)\n                        record[\"control_latency_ms\"] = baseline_record[\"latency_ms\"]\n                        record[\"control_samples_ms\"] = baseline_record[\"samples_ms\"]\n                        record[\"relative_cpu_time\"] = record[\"latency_ms\"] / baseline_record[\"latency_ms\"]\n                        record[\"case_index\"] = i\n                        per_case.append(record)\n                    records.append({\"seed\": seed, \"latency_ms\": statistics.mean(c[\"latency_ms\"] for c in per_case),\n                                    \"relative_cpu_time\": statistics.mean(c[\"relative_cpu_time\"] for c in per_case), \"cases\": per_case})\n        latency = statistics.mean(r[\"relative_cpu_time\"] for r in records)\n        anchor = protocol[\"baseline_ms\"]\n        if not args.raw_only and (anchor is None or anchor <= protocol[\"upper_bound_ms\"]):\n            raise Invalid(\"infrastructure_error\", \"Scoring anchors have not been calibrated.\")\n        score = None if args.raw_only else (anchor - latency) / (anchor - protocol[\"upper_bound_ms\"])\n        result = {\"status\": \"ok\", \"metric\": \"relative_process_cpu_time\", \"direction\": \"minimize\", \"raw_value\": latency,\n                  \"mean_candidate_cpu_ms\": statistics.mean(r[\"latency_ms\"] for r in records),\n                  \"score\": score, \"records\": records, \"quality_gates_passed\": True,\n                  \"method_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(args.method.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n                  \"protocol_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(args.protocol.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n                  \"protocol\": protocol[\"protocol\"], \"torch\": torch.__version__,\n                  \"start_unix\": started, \"end_unix\": time.time(), \"training\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\"}\n        atomic_json(args.output, result)\n        print(json.dumps(result, allow_nan=False), flush=True)\n        return 0\n    except Invalid as e:\n        result = {\"status\": e.kind, \"failure_reason\": e.message, \"score\": -1 if e.kind == \"hard_gate\" else None,\n                  \"start_unix\": started, \"end_unix\": time.time()}\n        atomic_json(args.output, result)\n        print(json.dumps(result), flush=True)\n        return 0 if e.kind == \"hard_gate\" else 1\n    except Exception as e:\n        result = {\"status\": \"infrastructure_error\", \"failure_reason\": f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\", \"score\": None,\n                  \"start_unix\": started, \"end_unix\": time.time()}\n        atomic_json(args.output, result)\n        print(json.dumps(result), flush=True)\n        return 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n\"\"\"Protected subprocess launcher; candidate receives tensors, never expected outputs.\"\"\"\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport statistics\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\n\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\ntorch.set_num_interop_threads(1)\nsource, input_path, output_path = map(Path, sys.argv[1:4])\ndata = np.load(input_path, allow_pickle=False)\nvalues = [torch.from_numpy(data[name].copy()) for name in (\"x\", \"wq\", \"wk\", \"wv\")]\nvalues.extend([float(data[\"alpha\"]), float(data[\"beta\"])])\nspec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"candidate_method\", source)\nmodule = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\nspec.loader.exec_module(module)\nsamples = []\nwall_samples = []\nwith torch.inference_mode():\n    for _ in range(int(data[\"warmup\"])):\n        module.attention(*values)\n    for _ in range(int(data[\"repeats\"])):\n        start_wall = time.perf_counter_ns()\n        start = time.process_time_ns()\n        output = module.attention(*values)\n        samples.append((time.process_time_ns() - start) / 1e6)\n        wall_samples.append((time.perf_counter_ns() - start_wall) / 1e6)\n    # A fresh call with fresh tensors also rejects stale cached outputs.\n    output = module.attention(*[v.clone() if isinstance(v, torch.Tensor) else v for v in values])\ninput_unchanged = all(torch.equal(v, torch.from_numpy(data[name])) for name, v in zip((\"x\", \"wq\", \"wk\", \"wv\"), values[:4]))\nif not isinstance(output, torch.Tensor):\n    print(json.dumps({\"worker_failure\":\"format_error\",\"message\":\"attention must return a Tensor\"}),flush=True)\n    raise SystemExit(3)\nif output.dtype != torch.float32 or output.device.type != \"cpu\":\n    print(json.dumps({\"worker_failure\":\"hard_gate\",\"message\":\"output must remain float32 CPU\"}),flush=True)\n    raise SystemExit(3)\nnp.savez(output_path, output=output.detach().numpy(), samples=np.array(samples, dtype=np.float64),\n         wall_samples=np.array(wall_samples, dtype=np.float64), input_unchanged=input_unchanged)\nprint(json.dumps({\"median_ms\": statistics.median(samples), \"pid\": os.getpid()}), flush=True)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
